  "content": {
    "title": "2026 Masters purse payout, breakdown. Winner gets $4.5 million payday",
    "text": "Updated April 11, 2026, 1:10 p.m. ETThe 2026 Masters purse is a record $22.5 million, with the winner receiving $4.5 million.Rory McIlroy was leading the tournament halfway through, seeking a back-to-back victory.Professional golfers who miss the cut still receive $25,000, while amateurs receive no prize money.In addition to prize money, the Masters champion receives a green jacket, a replica trophy, and a gold coin.If they aren't already, the Masters 2026 winner and runner-up will become multi-millionaires, taking home $4.5 million and $2.43 million, respectively.The Masters purse and payouts by place were released on Saturday, April 11, after the field was cut down to the top 50 players (including ties) following Friday's second round at Augusta National Golf Club.Rory McIlroy was in command of the 90th Masters halfway through the tournament, posting a record 12-under-par score after two rounds. If he wins this year, he would be in rare company as only the fourth player to win back-to-back green jackets.The 2026 Masters purse is a whopping $22.5 million, a record amount for the tournament. For comparison, the purse for 2025 was $21 million.In addition to the prize money and iconic green jacket, Masters champions take home a replica Masters trophy and a gold coin.Here's how much the 2026 Masters winner makes and the Masters payout by place:Masters players who miss the cut still get paidProfessional golfers who miss the cut at the Masters are paid $25,000 each.Do amateurs playing in Masters 2026 get paid?Amateurs who play in the Masters Tournament do not receive monetary prizes.The amateur with the lowest score at the end of the Tournament wins a silver cup. However, for the second year in a row, no amateur made the cut at the Masters.How much prize money will 2026 Masters winner get?The 2026 Masters winner will get a whopping $4.5 million payday. In 2025, Rory McIlroy won $4.2 million for his first Masters victory.Masters 2026 purse, payout by place, prize money distributionThe 2026 Masters purse is $22.5 million.Professional players who missed the cut will receive $25,000 each. Amateur players receive no monetary prizes.Here's the prize money breakdown by place:Pos. Player Total Payout$4,500,000$2,430,000$1,530,000$1,080,000$900,000$810,000$753,750$697,500$652,500$607,500$562,500$517,500$472,500$427,500$405,000$382,500$360,000$337,500$315,000$292,500$270,000$252,000$234,000$216,000$198,000$180,000$173,250$166,500$159,750$153,000$146,250$139,500$132,750$127,125$121,500$115,875$110,250$105,750$101,250$96,750$92,250$87,750$83,250$78,750$74,250$69,750$65,250$61,650$58,50056,700The remaining professionals will receive cash prizes ranging downward from $55,350 depending on their final score.Masters 2025 payout. How much did Rory McIlroy win?Here's how the then-record $21 million purse was distributed to players at the 2025 Masters Tournament:Pos. Player Total Payout1 Rory McIlroy -11 $4,200,0002 Justin Rose -11 $2,268,0003 Patrick Reed -9 $1,428,0004 Scottie Scheffler -8 $1,008,000T5 Sungjae Im -7 $798,000T5 Bryson DeChambeau -7 $798,0007 Ludvig Aberg -6 $703,500T8 Jason Day -5 $588,000T8 Corey Conners -5 $588,000T8 Xander Schauffele -5 $588,000T8 Zach Johnson -5 $588,000T12 Harris English -4 $462,000T12 Max Homa -4 $462,000T14 Bubba Watson -3 $336,000T14 Jon Rahm -3 $336,000T14 Jordan Spieth -3 $336,000T14 Tyrrell Hatton -3 $336,000T14 Matt McCarty -3 $336,000T14 Tom Hoge -3 $336,000T14 Collin Morikawa -3 $336,000T21 Hideki Matsuyama -2 $210,000T21 Davis Riley -2 $210,000T21 Tommy Fleetwood -2 $210,000T21 Daniel Berger -2 $210,000T21 Byeong Hun An -2 $210,000T21 Viktor Hovland -2 $210,000T27 Aaron Rai -1 $158,500T27 Michael Kim -1 $158,500T29 Sahith Theegala E $142,800T29 Denny McCarthy E $142,800T29 Joaquin Niemann E $142,800T32 Brian Campbell 1 $118,860T32 Maverick McNealy 1 $118,860T32 Rasmus Hojgaard 1 $118,860T32 Max Greyserman 1 $118,860T36 Justin Thomas 2 $118,860T36 Brian Harman 2 $96,600T36 Patrick Cantlay 2 $96,600T36 Charl Schwartzel 2 $96,600T40 Matt Fitzpatrick 3 $96,600T40 Nick Taylor 3 $84,000T42 Akshay Bhatia 4 $84,000T42 Danny Willett 4 $77,700T42 J.T. Poston 4 $77,700T42 Shane Lowry 4 $77,700T46 Wyndham Clark 5 $59,535T46 Sam Burns 5 $59,535T46 Davis Thompson 5 $59,53549 Min Woo Lee 6 $59,53550 J.J. Spaun 7 $52,92051 Nico Echavarria 8 $51,660T52 Stephan Jaeger 9 $51,660T52 Tom Kim 9 $51,660How much do caddies make at the Masters?Caddies are paid weekly wages plus a percentage of the player's tournament earnings, the Association of Professional Caddies and the Caddies Network told CBS News.Where to watch Round 3 and 4 of the 2026 MastersWatch the final two rounds of the 2026 Masters on Paramount+ (12-2 p.m. ET) and CBS/Paramount+ (2-7 p.m. ET).Kim Luciani is a journalist for the USA TODAY Network-Florida's Audience team. You can get all of Florida’s best content directly in your inbox each weekday by signing up for the free newsletter, Florida TODAY, at https://palmbeachpost.com/newsletters.",
